oxbrotli is written from the Brotli specification. It includes data from that
specification, and some numeric settings chosen to match the reference
implementation, credited here.


1. RFC 7932, "Brotli Compressed Data Format"
   J. Alakuijala and Z. Szabadka, July 2016
   https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7932

   Taken from the RFC's text by scripts/extract-rfc.py, and checked against the
   lengths and CRC-32s the RFC gives:

   - src/dictionary.bin: the static dictionary (Appendix A)
   - src/dictionary_tables.rs: the dictionary's word counts (NDBITS, Appendix
     A) and the 121 word transforms (Appendix B)
   - src/context_lut.rs: the context lookup tables (section 7.1)

   And from the RFC's tables: the insert, copy and block count codes
   (src/tables.rs, sections 5 and 6), the code length code order and lengths
   (section 3.5) and the initial distances (section 4).

